\begin{quotation}
In front of the player, there are three closed doors. Behind one of the doors, there is a prize of a new car, and behind the other two doors, there are goats, which mean losing the game. If the player chooses the door with the new car, they win it. After the player chooses one of the doors, the host Monty opens one of the remaining two doors that has a goat behind it.

Now, the player is asked if they want to switch to the other unopened door.
Should the player switch their choice of door at this point?
\end{quotation}
